TITLE:: PianoRollSidebar
SUMMARY:: Right-docked sidebar showing grid resolution and selection count for the piano roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollSidebar:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: fixed to the right edge of LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: (sibling of the roll LINK::Classes/ScrollView::, not inside the scroll canvas). It displays the current snap grid as a readable fraction (for example CODE::1/8 beat::), the number of selected notes, and compact keyboard hints for grid editing.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollSidebar::.

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for label colours.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: refresh
Updates the grid and selection labels. When CODE::pendingDenominator:: is non-nil, the grid label shows an in-progress entry (for example CODE::1/16?:: while the user holds G and types digits).

ARGUMENT:: gridDenominator
Integer denominator N for the active grid (resolution CODE::1/N:: beats).

ARGUMENT:: selectionCount
Number of currently selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

ARGUMENT:: pendingDenominator
Optional string of digits being entered during G-hold grid resolution entry; pass nil when not entering a new resolution.

PRIVATE:: init
